
I converted a 8GB single CSV file to parquet there it saves into multiple parquet files 
the reason is this how the spark will create partitons and change form one large csv to multiple parquet files for faster processing.

If you really want just one file (for portability or sharing), you can coalesce or repartition before writing:
python
# Coalesce to 1 partition (single file)
df.coalesce(1).write.mode("overwrite").parquet("/path/to/output_parquet")
coalesce(1) forces Spark to write everything into one file.

This can be inefficient for large datasets (like 8GB), because it removes parallelism and makes one executor handle all the data.


